# mtrxedit, the editor of binary arrays for tie-ups and liftplans (ipl_gpacks, weaving; built on the library's vidgets, a sibling of penelope):
# a new array of 10 by 6 through the tile menu's dialog, a cell set and a dragged row with the left button, a cell cleared with the right, a
# transformation button and its undo (meta z), one symmetry and a mirrored pair, the information box (meta i), the array written under a typed
# name through the file menu's dialog, quit (meta q). Cell j i of the 10 by 6 grid stands at 160+18j 70+18i. A dialog stands in the middle
# of the window and takes keys only with the pointer inside it.
# the tile menu held open, its item new; the two fields are typed over (the first stands selected, Tab goes to the second)
move 55 10
press 1
wait
move 60 30
release 1
wait
move 213 209
key BackSpace
type 10
key Tab
key BackSpace
type 6
wait
key Return
wait
# a cell, a dragged row, one cell of the row cleared with the right button
click 1 169 79
wait
drag 1 169 115 331 115
wait
click 3 241 115
wait
# the first transformation button, shift up; meta z undoes it
click 1 56 71
wait
keydown Alt_L
key z
keyup Alt_L
wait
# the last symmetry button, then one cell: it and its mirror are set
click 1 83 394
wait
click 1 187 151
wait
# meta i: the information box, closed with Return
move 213 209
keydown Alt_L
key i
keyup Alt_L
wait
key Return
wait
# the file menu held open, its item write: a dialog takes the file name
move 18 10
press 1
wait
move 30 45
release 1
wait
move 213 209
type t.tie
key Return
wait
# meta q ends the editor (the menu's own quit item cannot: its label carries a space the program's case does not)
keydown Alt_L
key q
keyup Alt_L
